# Full-source context qualification through v11

`full_context_profiles_v11_audit.json` is the additive cross-profile audit. It binds
41 retained evidence files and checks the results without changing earlier runs.

| Native source profile | Full XML preparation, seconds | Full Pyparsing producer process |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Unmodified v5 | 64.838 | Deadline at 600.203 seconds |
| Hoisted node CID index v7 | 26.296 | Deadline at 600.197 seconds |
| Fixed CID encoding v8 | 16.731 | Deadline at 600.196 seconds |
| CID syntax validation cache v9 | 7.793 | Deadline at 600.211 seconds |
| Escaped literal union v11 | 7.937 | Deadline at 600.202 seconds |

All five full XML native producer/consumer roundtrips pass, with exactly the same
state and semantic root. All five Pyparsing scans have the same state CID. The
table reports individual shared-host runs; it is not a replicated speedup estimate.

The deadline means the producer process did not finish. It does not establish
that bundle construction failed. In the separate v5 stage diagnostic the full
bundle was assembled and verified before the source-read stage. In v11 the producer
even wrote its result at 597.222 seconds before the 600-second process deadline.
Its full semantic root matches the independently built and verified full bundle.
No Pyparsing consumer was dispatched in these deadline runs, so no full Pyparsing
roundtrip is admitted through v11.

The literal-union change preserves the predicate that any ASCII node CID occurs
anywhere as a byte substring in the canonical link payload. Its 1,235 constructed
controls include embedded strings, escaped metacharacters, overlaps and empty
sets. An actual full-repository audit compares both predicates on all 55,859 links
against 3,957 node CIDs: every result is equal, and an embedded actual CID is
rejected. That audit also builds and verifies all 67,872 native bundle blocks.
The legacy and union predicates take 72.358 and 2.834 seconds within this diagnostic;
those subsets cannot be substituted for end-to-end service cost. All 64 existing
native content, Merkle, source and freshness regressions pass under this profile.

`requests_public_enrollment_v1/summary.json` separately qualifies both newly
exported public Requests development nodes. Each captures 97 files and scans all
35 Python files, yielding 863 symbols. The older and newer nodes retain 5,129,625
and 5,131,808 raw bytes respectively. Each native consumer materializes every raw
file and passes eleven binding/tampering controls. There are zero source omissions,
zero provider calls, no signed execution evidence and no token-savings result.
The generic repository-context API is available to the repair controller, but
changed accepted source needs a new capture and preparation.
